  "body": "In the spec, the two values of the IDL `boolean` type are currently written with `<code class=idl>` like \"`true`\". Yet the ECMAScript Boolean type values are written with `<emu-val>` like \"**true**\" in the same spec, and most other specs (e.g. the [URL Standard](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-urlsearchparams-has)) write boolean values without any particular styling like \"true\".\r\n\r\nIMO we should remove the `<code class=idl>` styling. The ES vs. IDL distinction is okay (maybe even preferred).",
